<title>GREECE: XIOSBANK KEEPS BUSINESS CREDIT UNCHANGED AT 19.75PCT.</title>
<headline>XIOSBANK KEEPS BUSINESS CREDIT UNCHANGED AT 19.75PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's private Xiosbank said it would keep its base business credit rate constant at 19.75 percent for a week effective Monday, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>XiosAlma deposit account will offer annual yields that reach up to 12.40 percent, it said. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
